WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mississippi Senator
Cindy Hyde-Smith

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.203 line:92%
made a campaign stop recently.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.305 size:78% position:39%
While she was there,
one of her supporters

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
said a lot of nice things
about her,

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.675 line:92%
and in response, she said,

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If he invited me
to a public hanging,

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.245 line:92%
I'd be on the front row,"

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
which many took
to be a reference to lynching.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, of course,
it's not appropriate

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.151
for a public official or anyone
to make a joke about lynching,

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:22.055
so here to comment is one of
our writers, Amber Ruffin.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:26.760 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-All aboard!

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.196 line:92%
-Amber, what are you doing?

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.065 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I'm driving the train.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.500 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And what train is that?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.768 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-The Redemption Train!

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:38.438
Now, sometimes, public officials
say crazy, racist things,

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that doesn't mean
they can't get back on track.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, all aboard
the Redemption Train!

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.414 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Train horn toots ]

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.681 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
All you have to do
is release a statement

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.986 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that says, "I'm sorry."

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:55.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
So Cindy Hyde-Smith
released one that said,

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:59.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Any attempt to turn this into
a negative connotation

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is ridiculous."

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.362 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.798 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Not exactly an apology,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
but she can still keep
the redemption train on track

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:12.539
by holding a press conference
where she acts really sorry.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.107 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Take it away, Senator!

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We put out
a statement yesterday,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.944 line:92%
and we stand by that statement.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm.
Try again.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We put out
this statement yesterday,

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.884
and it's available,
and we stand by that statement.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:25.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-N-Not quite.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:29.422
-We made a statement yesterday,
and we stand by the statement,

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's all
I'm going to say about it.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:36.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Repeat after me --
I'm sorry.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I put out
a statement yesterday,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's all
I'm gonna say about it.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.702 line:92%
-Uh-oh, this is not going great.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:43.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We're overheating.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.839 line:92%
Someone needs to do something.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:46.906 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Get the governor!

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can tell you,
all of us in public life

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.376 line:92%
have said things on occasion

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we
could have phrased better.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you make as many speeches
as we do in public life,

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that does occur.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.651 line:92%
-Hey, that's a great point.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know this woman,
and I know her heart.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:03.356
I knew it when I appointed her.
I know it now.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:06.359 size:75% position:38%
She meant no offense
by that statement.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:09.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nothing but
smooth sailing ahead.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.397
-Brought the President of
the United States here

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:14.200 line:92%
to open the Civil Rights Museum.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.268 line:92%
And African-American leadership

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would fail
to even come to the event

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the President of
the United States was there.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:24.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-oh. I would not bring up
Donald Trump right now.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.313 line:92%
We're going off the rails here.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.215 line:92%
This could not get any worse.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Today, I talked about
the genocide

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
of over 20 million
African-American children.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:37.157
-Why's this man
talking about dead black kids?!

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, in my heart,
I am confused about

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.393 size:88% position:44% line:92%
where the outrage is at,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:43.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
about 20 million
African-American children

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.230 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that have been aborted.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one wants
to say anything about that.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.168 line:92%
No one wants to talk about that.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What the [bleep] is he
talking about abortion for?!

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What the hell
is going on up here?!

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's trying
to make it about abortion!

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.678 line:92%
-This train is going to explode!

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.613 line:92%
-You think I don't know that?!

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.815 line:92%
I'm doing everything I can!

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.517 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Senator, save us!

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I put out
a statement yesterday.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.587 size:81% position:41% line:92%
A statement yesterday.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
A statement.
A statement.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:09.722 size:81% position:41% line:92%
A statement yesterday.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
Statement.
Statement.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.192 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Statement yesterday.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.359 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Stop saying that!

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We have to fix this!
-We can't!

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.497 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-What about her career?!

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's a white lady
from Mississippi!

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
She'll be fine!
Save yourself!

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.304 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm gonna jump!

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.240 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Aaaaah!!

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Explosion ]

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.644 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:37.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sometimes, not even the
Redemption Train can save you.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.118 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Unh!

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.887 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:41.888 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-She's gone.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.756 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

